From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Skin Fixer Tooling <tooling@skinfixer.local>
Date: Sun, 23 Aug 2026 08:45:26 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat: workspace inspector, add-to-current-scene

Gives the workspace object real controls, and makes it possible to add the rig
to a scene you already have rather than generating a fresh one.

New:
- SkinFixerWorkspaceEditor: custom inspector for the workspace object. Lists
  every skinned renderer under the Models root with vertex and bone counts,
  warns when a mesh is not readable, and opens the Weight Editor already bound
  to a chosen renderer. Key, fill and rim intensity sliders plus a rig rotation
  slider sit alongside, since raking the key light across a joint is the fastest
  way to spot a collapsing silhouette. Raw component references stay available
  behind a foldout.

Changed:
- WorkspaceSceneBuilder gains Add Workspace To Current Scene. It adopts an
  existing main camera and the first directional light instead of leaving
  duplicates behind, so a stock Unity scene converts cleanly. All adopted
  objects are recorded for undo.
- BuildContents takes an adoptExisting flag; camera and key light creation now
  reuse rather than always constructing.
- SkinWeightToolsWindow.ShowWindow returns the window, and a new OpenWith
  binds it to a renderer directly.
